---
const preguntas = [
  ["Which agents can use it?", "Any agent that supports the Agent Skills standard and can run shell commands: Claude Code, Codex, Gemini CLI, Cursor, GitHub Copilot in VS Code and many more. In a chat without a terminal (for example claude.ai) it can draft documentation, but the chat has no access to your repository, so it can't keep docs verified."],
  ["Does my code leave my machine?", "No. DocKeeper makes no network calls. The seal file contains file paths, line numbers and hashes, never code."],
  ["Do I need an AI model to run the check?", "No. Your agent uses the skill to write documentation; the check itself is plain Python and runs anywhere, including CI."],
  ["What happens when I rename a function?", "Anchors to it report <code>CHANGED</code> (symbol not found). Update the anchor in the document and run <code>dockeeper scan</code>."],
  ["What should I commit?", "Your documents, <code>.dockeeper.json</code> if you use one, and <code>.dockeeper.sello.json</code>, the seal that CI checks against."],
  ["Is the CLI in English?", "Its messages are in Spanish today. Verdict codes and the <code>--json</code> output are stable, so agents and scripts are not affected."],
];
---
<section id="faq">
  <div class="wrap">
    <p class="eyebrow">FAQ</p>
    <h2>Questions</h2>
    <div class="faq">
      {preguntas.map(([pregunta, respuesta]) => <details><summary>{pregunta}</summary><p set:html={respuesta} /></details>)}
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
